{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen-1788286075-T27CMgj6W8xwc4Ir2DV3","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The verdict is written to `.llm/runs/fix-dev-probe-startup-budget--1868/impl-eval-verdict.md` (untracked — detached HEAD; nothing else touched or committed). Printed:\n\n---\n\n# IMPL-EVAL verdict — PR #1883 / issue #1868\n\n## PASS_IMPL\n\n**Head judged:** `5bfd7c6beb54166a7adf1aa55bb3bdc6fa9ab513` (matches PR #1883 `head.sha`).\n\n**Evaluator identity (requested vs observed):** Lane `formal_impl_evaluation`, open-model route per `.llm/harness/workflow/lane-policy.md:181` — requested `z-ai/glm-5.3-flash`, effort `max`. Observed: model `z-ai/glm-5.3-flash`; effort `max` confirmed from the launcher process command line (`deno task agentic:claude-openrouter --model z-ai/glm-5.3-flash --effort max`). No mismatch. Session separation holds — this session wrote no product code and did not supervise the implementation.\n\n## Findings\n\n| # | Question | Verdict | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| D1 | Genuinely phase-aware? | **CONFIRMED** | `probe-project-boundary-dev.ts:1-5` exports `DEV_STARTUP_BUDGET_MS=180_000` / `FRESH_HTTP_READINESS_BUDGET_MS=60_000`; the 60 s HTTP deadline is computed only **after** the Vite `'Local:'` marker ends the 180 s startup phase (`:27-54`). End-to-end, 65 s fixture preflight (> the whole old 60 s budget): pre-fix → `exit=1 elapsed=61s`, `Fresh dev server failed under hostile parent tsconfig: fetch failed; status=running` (misclassification reproduced); head → `exit=0 elapsed=66s`, `Fresh dev server answered 200`. Anti-vacuousness: a reconstructed single raised-constant implementation fails the committed suite (`exit 1; 2 passed, 1 failed` — the slow-preflight case, `Fresh dev server failed: server did not answer`). |\n| D2 | Prompt child-exit? | **CONFIRMED** | Focused test passes (`status=23`, `startup/preflight` in message, `sleepCalls===1`, no fetch). End-to-end: `Deno.exit(5)` child → `exit=1 elapsedMs=134`, `Generated dev process exited during startup/preflight; status=5`. `childStatus` is raced in both phases; exit preempts in-flight sleeps. |\n| D3 | Truthful timeout output? | **CONFIRMED** | Three distinct head messages observed by execution: `Generated dev process exited during startup/preflight; status=5` (134 ms); `Fresh dev server exited after startup under hostile parent tsconfig; status=1` (child died after banner); `Fresh dev server failed under hostile parent tsconfig after startup: fetch failed; status=running` after the full 60 s readiness budget (`elapsed=60s`). Startup timeout (`Generated dev startup/preflight timed out after Nms; status=running`) proven by focused test 3, which asserts the message does **not** contain `Fresh dev server failed`. |\n| D4 | RED genuine, non-vacuous, zero product files? | **CONFIRMED** | `git show cd2337d36 --name-only`: 9 run artifacts + the test file only. Extracted via `git archive` into `.llm/tmp/eval-1868/red-tree`: **exit 1, 0 passed / 3 failed / 3 total, uniqueFailures=1** — exactly the PR's claim. Failure mode: pre-fix probe is an unguarded top-level script; import hits `generated project root and app name are required`. Non-vacuous beyond the missing seam (see D1); RED→GREEN test diff only injects the fake clock, no assertion weakened. |\n| D5 | Real sleeps for production timeouts? | **CONFIRMED (no)** | No `setTimeout` in the committed test — clock/sleep injected; full-budget sleep short-circuited to a pending promise. Measured runtimes: 710 ms (head), 593 ms (RED), 674 ms (naive variant) — vs 180 s. |\n| D6 | Ceiling and lock? | **CONFIRMED** (one REFUSAL) | PR range = exactly 11 files (9 run artifacts + probe + test). `git rev-parse origin/main:deno.lock HEAD:deno.lock` → `ac2ee042…` both sides, byte-identical (`origin/main`=`302409f0c`, at/after `102ef8a10`). Gates run myself: focused test 3 passed/0 failed; `e2e/tests` gate **203 passed / 0 failed**; scoped check 188 files 0 diagnostics; scoped fmt 188 files 0 findings. Scoped lint → **REFUSAL** (`Package 'zod' not found in catalog`, 7 detached `fixtures/desktop-native/` files) — recorded as REFUSAL, never PASS/FAIL; pre-existing verified (`git diff --stat origin/main 5bfd7c6be -- packages/cli/e2e/fixtures/` is empty). |\n| D7 | Verifier / dependency-closure absorbed? | **CONFIRMED (no)** | No file outside probe/test/artifacts in the range. Dev-chain spawn args, cwd, and port `5199` identical to pre-fix (block moved under `runProbe`, indentation only). |\n\n## What I tried that failed to break it\n\n1. **\"Just a bigger number\"** — rebuilt the fix as one 180 s shared deadline (same seam): the committed suite fails it 1/3. The shipped implementation passes 3/3.\n2. **Slow-preflight end-to-end** — 65 s preflight: pre-fix misclassifies at 61 s; head succeeds at 66 s through the real `import.meta.main` entry point.\n3. **Prompt-exit regression** — immediate-exit child fails in 134 ms with the true status; a child dying after the banner reports as exit-during-readiness (status=1), not a fetch failure.\n4. **Message-parser coupling** — no external parser of the old message exists (only the gate-name constant and the invocation path in `database-gates.ts:212`).\n5. **Test-1 microtask determinism** — the fake clock lands between iterations; the in-flight poll sleep cannot exhaust the startup deadline before `startup.resolve()` is observed, and the full-budget sleep guard turns a shared-deadline implementation into a failure, not a silent pass.\n6. **Scope-creep sweep** and **lock drift** — none; blob-identical lock.\n7. **Coverage hole** — the focused test is outside `packages/cli/e2e/tests/`, but root `deno task test` discovery runs it (proven: `1 passed … 3907 filtered out` from the scaffold test path), so CI's `test` gate covers it.\n\n## Explicitly not evaluated (not a FAIL reason)\n\n`deno task e2e:cli` was **not run** — no runtime lease, and the brief prohibits it. Hosted CI owns the `scaffold.runtime` Flow-B/NAS acceptance; absence of a runtime receipt here is not a failure finding.\n\n## Blocking findings\n\nNone.\n\n## Non-blocking observations\n\n1. **Unbounded first fetch in the readiness phase** — a fetch that connects but never settles would stall past the 60 s deadline (deadline re-checked only after the race settles). Same shape as pre-fix; my readiness run ended at exactly 60 s. Future hardening: per-attempt `AbortSignal.timeout`.\n2. **`stopChild` catch breadth** — tolerates `Deno.errors.NotFound`, but Deno 2.9.5 throws `TypeError: Child process has already terminated` (observed in the pre-fix run). The `childExited` guard (set before the derived status promise settles) closes all normal paths; only a microtask-boundary race could mask an already-failing error. No false-PASS path.\n3. **`'Local:'` marker heuristic** — earlier output containing `Local:` would hand time to the readiness budget early; strictly more permissive than pre-fix, no false-failure risk.\n4. **Test 2's `sleepCalls === 1`** is implementation-coupled (deliberate documentation of the exit-wins property).\n5. **Root e2e lint REFUSAL** (desktop-native `zod` catalog) — pre-existing, PR-independent, recorded as REFUSAL only.\n\n---\n\n**Basis:** two genuinely independent budgets, exit preemption with real status in ~135 ms, distinct truthful messages for every failure mode, an exact non-vacuous RED (0/3), no production-timeout sleeps, an 11-file ceiling with a byte-identical lock, and no absorbed verifier/dependency-closure work. Three brief gates green; the lint refusal is the documented pre-existing baseline.","citations":[]}],"model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"inference_geo":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null,"speed":"standard"},"provider":"Parasail